<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adam Baldridge</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1685–1697</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adam Baldridge was an English former pirate who from 1691 ran a fortified trading post on Île Sainte-Marie off the north-east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>. Backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> merchants, notably Frederick Philipse, he sold supplies, liquor and arms to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> operating in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> and bought their plunder and enslaved captives. He left the island in 1697 after a local uprising and returned to New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york-maine">York</a>.</p></div>
